userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A bad (maximally unbalanced) partition immediately followed by a good one costs Θ(n) for the pair and leaves subproblems of essentially the same size as a single good partition — so alternating bad and good splits still gives O(n lg n).
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A bad split absorbed into the next good split costs the same Θ(n) and leaves the same subproblem sizes as one good split alone — so alternating bad and good partitions changes only the constant, not the O(n lg n) running time.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

